# The "far" cube in the two-cube overlap demo: center (0.15, 0.1, 0.4),
# half-size 0.55. Larger and farther from the camera than cube_near.obj,
# but their (x, y) footprints overlap on screen -- which is the whole
# point: only per-pixel depth testing can tell which one is actually in
# front at each overlapping pixel.
v -0.4 -0.45 -0.15
v 0.7 -0.45 -0.15
v 0.7 0.65 -0.15
v -0.4 0.65 -0.15
v -0.4 -0.45 0.95
v 0.7 -0.45 0.95
v 0.7 0.65 0.95
v -0.4 0.65 0.95
f 1 4 3
f 1 3 2
f 5 6 7
f 5 7 8
f 1 2 6
f 1 6 5
f 4 8 7
f 4 7 3
f 1 5 8
f 1 8 4
f 2 3 7
f 2 7 6
